{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_24633907624715683fc04b6f82804512c790651f2cd5ffc5fd1ed56ad889640a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c86da42dabae027be2cd17ad3465ecf6a352c740b2e886166e2b0af83c5d4ea","slc_7d792ba1395fcdd4773ed03f791c173a90a4a6b8b40881e309fd9da3c1044b32"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"The architecture targets zero runtime dependencies except googleapis; the gws module is a thin ~600-LOC CLI over googleapis, with MCP, GAM, gcalcli, gmailctl, and the official Rust gws CLI evaluated and rejected for v1.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b3c9776c318f3a63ad61fc96b1fb72d05df66813fa51ecd26475d0fd6c13ed3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15b31a5fc2c373a5c780ee1c0d16476935e53ada6b4882a2896310f99ed95556","slc_ea6011d7a09b18ae5a95907f028f262a7d75bb39effe60089c8478ec784899cf"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"Vault notes carry mandatory frontmatter provenance fields on every auto-write, including id, type, origin, source_sessions, confidence, recurrence, and a derived_from_untrusted flag.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5084cbc38fbf325c2c253449fe2129491a83eb5d8564e4e063c78cd081dd5538","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_20e0496fbeffe965385adffd1091d8f8a2fec6086c5719ba5b859757820028f8"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"The system map shows a canonical core at ~/.wienerdog/ (config.yaml, skills, prompts, bin, state, secrets, logs, install manifest) plus Claude and Codex adapters that sync compiles into ~/.claude/ and ~/.codex/.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_588a8d3d19f7c73c174d2be20e1be32aa845e54e212ff82119ecb5e6f49b7f02","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f50a7c202a5a24c9f628b8ff0f3f7b98bcd4096439e89238b2cb604666286f6f"],"source_ids":["src_1e938f9bf0f7506d8cee75f5bd66b684"],"text":"Repository development practice: the repo dogfoods its own product — its memory vault lives in memory/, its development conventions are its own CLAUDE.md, and most code is written by mid-tier AI models following its spec system in docs/specs/.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6322c2e1d5d04d702f592aece3185e18c01908b2aaaff66f52f3b9d7ecb1e9a4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a2c5a4d0006beacbc37c4b02750fbe9fc492776ac3bf9a459a4233bb3465685b","slc_a2ec7261448d084369c5df9b3a991adcd29239031f7d1dfbe4acb12c7c69a108","slc_b10ca1a9632c3dcf884d35327ce249313e137679d92181337e76541b848a850b"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"Scheduled jobs use OS-native schedulers (launchd, systemd user timers, Task Scheduler) invoking short-lived run-job processes with watchdog timeout, rotated logging, catch-up, and fail-loud alerting; the design explicitly uses no daemon.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_63cca3a57de5d309700d1ff247d0d31033b7b0badf369524eff9c42c4d45ef5f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e5e3a02a8638154f50db4d027f6ae33b6d8e873de24b94d818d200e9514fdf2d"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"Wienerdog never owns the user's CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md; it manages only a sentinel-delimited block, sync overwrites edits inside sentinels while leaving outside edits untouched, and uninstall removes exactly that region.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_688e4420a3e8bdb088dae1abc6c337a7b52584abfc71f3ef5fe3b4b9821638d4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"wienerdog-ai/wienerdog@91668da62822 snapshot 10c545f38401b46b","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ab59251f31b13643b5b20caf5c40e3210b64503537b2e5ca3b2b877a45653e84"],"source_ids":["src_006c0cd9cbd35cd98e0ab4656a4191f3"],"text":"Memory promotion uses tiered quality gates: daily logs need score >= 0.5, atomic notes >= 0.75, and Tier 3 (identity, preferences, skills, digest-fed content) requires score >= 0.85, recurrence across 3+ distinct sessions, and derived_from_untrusted false.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:31:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e7231624ba1f4c6fa1b7d180bc3cd167"}
